s in Natural Language Processing\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2023","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Is ChatGPT Good at Search? Investigating Large Language Models as Re-Ranking Agents","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b61","section_path_id":"1~7","quote":"[61]","offset":628}]},{"raw_text":"The cognitive science of science: Explanation, discovery, and conceptual change\n\t\t\n\t\t\tThagard\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2012\n\t\t\tThe MIT Press","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b62","section_path_id":"5.1","quote":"62]","offset":131}]},{"raw_text":"DORIS-MAE: scientific document retrieval using multi-level aspect-based queries\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJianyouWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKaichengWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tXiaoyueWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tPrudhvirajNaidu\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLeonBergen\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tRamamohanPaturi\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tProceedings of the 37th International Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n\t\tthe 37th International Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2023","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"DORIS-MAE: scientific document retrieval using multi-level aspect-based queries","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b63","section_path_id":"1~6","quote":"63]","offset":327}]},{"raw_text":"LLMFactor: Extracting profitable factors through prompts for explainable stock movement prediction\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMeiyunWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKiyoshiIzumi\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHirokiSakaji\n\t\t\n\t\tarXiv:2406.10811\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2024. 2024\n\t\t\n\t\n\tarXiv preprint","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"2406.10811","title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b64","section_path_id":"1~19","quote":"[64]","offset":319}]},{"raw_text":"QingyunWang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDougDowney\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJiHeng\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTomHope\n\t\t\n\t\tarXiv:2305.14259\n\t\tScimon: Scientific inspiration machines optimized for novelty\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2023. 2023\n\t\t\n\t\n\tarXiv preprint","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"2305.14259","title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b65","section_path_id":"5.3","quote":"65]","offset":74}]},{"raw_text":"Creative Computing: an approach to knowledge combination for creativity?\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHongjiYang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tDelinJing\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLuZhang\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\t2016 IEEE Symposium on Service-Oriented System Engineering (SOSE)\n\t\t\n\t\t\tIEEE\n\t\t\t2016","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"Creative Computing: an approach to knowledge combination for creativity?","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b66","section_path_id":"5.3","quote":"66]","offset":217}]},{"raw_text":"Self-alignment for factuality: Mitigating hallucinations in llms via self-evaluation\n\t\t\n\t\t\tXiaoyingZhang\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tBaolinPeng\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tYeTian\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tJingyanZhou\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLifengJin\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tLinfengSong\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHaitaoMi\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\tHelenMeng\n\t\t\n\t\tarXiv:2402.09267\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2024. 2024\n\t\t\n\t\n\tarXiv preprint","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"2402.09267","title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b67","section_path_id":"1~19","quote":"[67]","offset":271}]},{"raw_text":"Input: The idea text + 𝑘 top-ranked similar papers from the retrieval pipeline. Task: Write a 60-100 word review comparing the idea to the retrieved papers, then classify as Novel or Not Novel. Novelty definitions: Not Novel-closely replicates existing work with minimal new contributions. Novel-introduces new concepts/approaches not common in literature; or uniquely combines existing concepts in a way no retrieved paper does; or applies the same approach to a genuinely new domain. In-context learning: Expert-labeled (idea, papers, review, classification) tuples are injected-the same examples shown in Appendix C.2. Multi-turn structure: Uses a simulated dialogue (user → assistant → user) to first present the idea\n\t\t\n\t\n\t3.4 Assess Idea Novelty. noveltyChecker(idea, similar_papers, expert_examples) Role: ReviewerGPT (system message then inject each retrieved paper as a separate user message-ensuring the model attends to each paper individually. Output: Class: [novel / not novel] followed by Review: The idea is [novel / not novel] because..","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Input: The original idea (short + long versions), the prior work it overlaps with, the novelty review explaining why it is not novel, and the full set of available facets in the user&apos;s workspace. Task: Generate 3 alternative ideas, each created by swapping exactly one facet: (1) Remove one purpose\n\t\t\n\t\n\tGenerate More-Novel Idea Suggestions. moreNovelIdea(idea, overlapping_papers, available_facets) Trigger: Called when the novelty checker classifies an idea as &quot;Not Novel","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Remove one mechanism, add a different mechanism","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]},{"raw_text":"Output per option: Removed facet (text + ID), added facet (text + ID), revised idea (100-150 words), justification of novelty, justification of usefulness. Design rationale: By constraining edits to a single facet swap, suggestions remain close to the user&apos;s original intent while systematically exploring the facet space for novelty\n\t\t\n\t\n\tSame quality requirements as the generation prompts ( §H.2.1)","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[]}],"layout_json":null,"tei_xml":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<TEI xml:space=\"preserve\" xmlns=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" \nxmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" \nxsi:schemaLocation=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kermitt2/grobid/master/grobid-home/schemas/xsd/Grobid.xsd\"\n xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">\n\t<teiHeader xml:lang=\"en\">\n\t\t<fileDesc>\n\t\t\t<titleStmt>\n\t\t\t\t<title level=\"a\" type=\"main\">Scideator: Human-LLM Compound System for Scientific Ideation through Facet Recombination and Novelty Evaluation</title>\n\t\t\t</titleStmt>\n\t\t\t<publicationStmt>\n\t\t\t\t<publis